  "starterCode": "# KV Head Repeat — reconstructed educational contract\nimport numpy as np\n\ndef solution(kv, num_query_heads):\n    # TODO: implement the operation described in the problem statement\n    pass\n",
  "solution": "### 💡 Intuition & Approach\nThe implementation computes **KV Head Repeat** by following direct architectural principles, leveraging vectorized operations to ensure both correctness and optimal runtime efficiency.\n\n### ⚡ Python Reference Implementation\n```python\nimport numpy as np\ndef solution(kv, num_query_heads):\n    kv=np.asarray(kv)\n    n=kv.shape[-3]\n    if n==0 or num_query_heads%n: raise ValueError(\"query heads must be divisible by KV heads\")\n    return np.repeat(kv,num_query_heads//n,axis=-3).tolist()\n```\n\n### ⏱️ Complexity Analysis\n- **Time Complexity**: $\\mathcal{O}(N)$ where $N$ represents the primary sequence length or dimension.\n- **Space Complexity**: $\\mathcal{O}(N)$ auxiliary memory for computing and storing output representations.",
